=== 1. BRAND DESIGN SYSTEM ===

Create a consistent design system for GuruAI.

Brand personality:
- Educational, modern, trustworthy, friendly, fast.
- Not childish, not overly corporate.
- Designed for students who want quick, clear answers.

Color palette:
- Primary brand color: indigo/blue, for example #4F46E5 or #2563EB.
- Primary CTA: same brand color.
- Background: #0B1120 for dark theme, #F8FAFC for light theme.
- Chat panel: #111827 dark / #FFFFFF light.
- Bot bubble: #1E293B dark / #F1F5F9 light.
- User bubble: brand color with white text.
- Secondary text: #94A3B8 dark / #64748B light.
- Border: #1F2937 dark / #E2E8F0 light.
- Success: #16A34A
- Warning: #F59E0B
- Error: #DC2626
- Premium/gold accent: #F59E0B for upgrade badges and premium plans.
- Maintain at least 4.5:1 text contrast in both themes.

Typography:
- Font: Inter or system-ui.
- Chat text: 16px minimum.
- Small labels: 14px minimum.
- Header title: 18–20px.
- Buttons: 15–16px.
- Line height: 1.5.
- No tiny, low-contrast text.

Shape and spacing:
- Spacing scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32px.
- Message bubbles: 16px radius.
- Buttons: 12px radius.
- Input field: 16px radius.
- Cards: 16px radius.
- Use subtle shadows and clean borders.
- Avoid visual clutter.

=== 2. DESKTOP UI LAYOUT ===

Create a full-page AI chat application layout.

Desktop structure:
- Left sidebar: 280px, collapsible.
- Main chat area: flexible width, centered content, maximum readable width 900–1100px.
- Right panel: optional, only for model details, usage limit, sources, attachments, or premium upgrade.
- Header: fixed at top, 64px height.
- Composer: fixed at bottom.

Desktop header:
- Left:
  - GuruAI logo/avatar.
  - “GuruAI” title.
  - Subtitle: “by HarshGuruJi”.
- Center:
  - Current model name, for example: “Guru-Flash 1.1”.
- Right buttons, in this order:
  1. New chat — plus icon.
  2. Search chats — magnifier icon.
  3. Chat history — clock icon.
  4. Preferences/settings — gear icon.
  5. Theme switcher — sun/moon icon.
  6. User account — avatar icon.
- Show request counter near the user area:
  - Guest: “8 requests left”
  - Member: “20 requests / 12h left”
- If requests are low, show a subtle warning badge: “Limited requests left”.

Desktop sidebar:
- Top:
  - Large “+ New Chat” primary button.
- Middle:
  - Recent chats list.
  - Each item: chat title, short preview, time.
  - Hover options: rename, pin, delete.
- Bottom:
  - Active model selector.
  - Theme selector: Dark, Slate Light, Clean Cyberpunk.
  - Sign in / user profile.
  - Upgrade to Premium button.
  - Help & Support.
  - Link to HarshGuruJi website.

Desktop chat area:
- Empty state:
  - GuruAI mascot or logo.
  - Heading: “Namaste! Main GuruAI hoon.”
  - Subheading: “Koi bhi sawaal poochho — study, coding, GK ya general knowledge.”
  - 4 quick-start buttons:
    - “Photosynthesis samjhao”
    - “Coding doubt clear karo”
    - “Essay likhne me help karo”
    - “Daily study plan banao”
- Messages:
  - Bot messages left-aligned with GuruAI avatar.
  - User messages right-aligned.
  - Maximum bubble width: 70% of chat area.
  - Support Markdown, lists, tables, code blocks, links, and images.
  - Code blocks must have language label and Copy Code button.
  - Auto-scroll to the latest message.
  - Show “Scroll to latest” floating button when user scrolls up.

Bot response actions:
- Below each bot response, show small icon buttons:
  - Copy
  - Regenerate
  - Like
  - Dislike
  - Share
- Each button must have tooltip and accessible label.
- Minimum clickable area: 32x32px on desktop, 44x44px on mobile.

Desktop composer:
- Sticky at bottom.
- Layout:
  - Left: attachment button.
  - Left: image/vision button if the selected model supports it.
  - Center: text input.
  - Right: microphone button.
  - Right: send button.
- Placeholder: “Apna sawaal GuruAI se poochhein…”
- Enter sends message.
- Shift + Enter adds a new line.
- While response is generating:
  - Send button becomes Stop button.
  - Show animated typing indicator.
  - Prevent duplicate submissions.
- Above composer, show horizontally scrollable quick replies:
  - “Explain in simple Hindi”
  - “Make notes”
  - “Give examples”
  - “Solve step by step”
  - “Translate to English”
- Show selected model and remaining requests subtly above or beside composer.

