=== 7. STATES — HANDLE ALL ===

Empty state:
- Friendly welcome.
- Bot capabilities.
- 4 starter prompts.
- Input visible.

Loading state:
- GuruAI avatar with animated typing dots.
- Text: “GuruAI soch raha hai…”
- Stop generation button.
- Skeleton loading for long answers.

Error state:
- Friendly message: “Kuch galat ho gaya. Kripya dobara try karein.”
- Retry button.
- Report issue button.
- Human support link to HarshGuruJi contact page.

Limit reached state:
- Clear limit message.
- Upgrade CTA.
- Sign-in CTA for guests.

Offline state:
- Banner: “Aap offline hain. Message send nahi ho sakta.”
- Retry option.

Model unavailable state:
- Message: “Ye model abhi available nahi hai.”
- Suggest switching to Guru-Flash 1.1.
- Model selector shortcut.

=== 8. ACCESSIBILITY ===

- Every icon button must have aria-label.
- Use semantic HTML: header, main, aside, footer, button, input.
- Keyboard navigation must work: Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Escape.
- Visible focus rings.
- Minimum mobile tap target: 44x44px.
- Text contrast minimum 4.5:1.
- Screen reader must announce:
  - “GuruAI is typing”
  - “Message sent”
  - “Response copied”
  - “Request limit reached”
  - “Error occurred”
- Support dark mode, light mode, and Clean Cyberpunk theme.
- Respect reduced-motion preference.

=== 9. RESPONSIVE RULES ===

- 320px: compact full-screen chat, no sidebar, simplified header.
- 375px: standard mobile layout.
- 640px: larger touch targets and comfortable spacing.
- 768px: tablet layout; sidebar becomes a drawer.
- 1024px: sidebar visible, wider chat area.
- 1440px: centered chat container, maximum content width 900–1100px.
- Use flexbox and CSS grid.
- No fixed pixel width for the main chat area.
- Test long Hindi/English messages, code blocks, images, attachments, emojis, keyboard-open state, landscape mode, and large font sizes.

